{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790468576,"nonce":"Paydr7wu20ukuYsDBh30CzpJmD0=","title":"Linked plugin calls: instances, Value, Buffer and Enum casts","message":"A Haxe program built for wasm calls a linked plugin's statics directly, with scalars and strings cast at the boundary (caribou 44b46f0, d4b7839; test crates/caribou-driver/tests/linked.rs). aot::host_link leaves every other member on the run-time path, and in a wasm module that path raises, because no library is loaded.\n\nStill to cast:\n- Plugin instances. A constructor (`c`) returns a Box the Haxe face must hold, and a method (`m`) takes that receiver. This needs a cast between the face object and the plugin's pointer, plus the drop hook.\n- `Value` (TypeTag::VALUE): a core value to a Haxe dynamic and back. The casts exist in proto (value_to_dyn / dyn_to_value) but have no link-shaped entry points yet.\n- `Buffer` / `BufferMut` and `haxe.io.Bytes`, as views and not copies.\n- `Enum\u003cT\u003e` to the Haxe enum and back (data::enum_to_haxe).\n\nEach needs a cast pair in caribou-ash/src/link.rs and an arm in aot::word_of. The Bridge must also declare the native's type as the program's own wherever the cast needs it, as it does for String since 38e4aff.","files":null}]}